From 11b5428ca112bb4331d67036fa2557463443799d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Lopez <slp@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:45:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bump imago to 0.2.6

Imago 0.2.6 includes a fix that prevents truncating a raw file when
there's a discard request pointing to the end of the file.

Fixes: #949

Signed-off-by: Sergio Lopez <slp@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit d166df9a80948d3017315d46b4822f203b1d01da)
Signed-off-by: Sergio Lopez <slp@redhat.com>

[steamac: from libkrun/libkrun PR #980 (the open 1.19.8 cherry-picks),
rebased onto v1.19.6; only the Cargo.toml context differs.
imago 0.2.3 shrinks raw images when discard or write-zeroes reaches the
last byte (libkrun/libkrun#949). steamos.img keeps the backup GPT after
home: this hardens future guest-wide discard and Reclaim Disk Space
(steamac#78), rather than fixing observed loss on steamac's layout.]
